&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most growth teams don&#39;t lack ideas. They lack the infrastructure to test them fast enough to matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring an Agentic Operator whose core output is one thing: reducing the time between hypothesis and signal. You&#39;ll build the agent pipelines, orchestration layers, and automation systems that let our growth team run more experiments in parallel — and learn from them faster — than any traditionally-staffed team could.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role. You&#39;ll treat AI agents as a programmable workforce, replacing human bottlenecks in the experimentation loop with systems that pre-validate, instrument, execute, and surface insights automatically. You won&#39;t be handed a playbook. You&#39;ll write it in code. You&#39;ll report to the Director of Demand Generation and work closely with channel owners, lifecycle, product, and sales to make the growth team&#39;s experiments faster, more rigorous, and more evidence-based.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person is operationally sharp with genuine growth instincts. You understand B2B SaaS funnels well enough to prioritize experiments intelligently and catch flawed hypotheses before they waste the team&#39;s time. You&#39;re technically fluent enough to build AI workflows, instrument experiments, and own the tracking systems the team depends on. And you bring the organizational discipline to manage a high-velocity experiment backlog without letting things slip through the cracks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Build&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Agent Pipelines for Concept Pre-Validation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before human resources touch a test, your agents have already scored it — LLM-evaluated copy variants, synthetic audience testing, funnel drop-off analysis. Only the strongest hypotheses make it to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;An Automated Experiment Queue&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the full loop: intake, prioritization, instrumentation, and readout — all accelerated via automation. Funnel drop-off doesn&#39;t trigger a Monday meeting; it triggers the next test.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;An Experimentation Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the full loop — backlog, sequencing, instrumentation, and readout — with the rigor to match. Every test ships with a falsifiable hypothesis, clean measurement setup, and defined success metric. Null results get documented, not buried. Channel owners, lifecycle, and PLG stay in sync so the team is always running the highest-leverage tests without conflicts or duplication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stack Orchestration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You wire together our existing tools — Amplitude, HubSpot, Clay, REO.dev and enrichment layers — so signals flow automatically into action. You integrate frontier LLMs (Claude, GPT) and workflow tools (n8n, Gumloop) into production-grade systems that improve over t

&lt;article&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Senior Manager, Brand Marketing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CircleCI helps more than two million developers ship software confidently. The way software gets built and shipped is getting turned on its head, and our brand has to meet the moment. It has a clear center: the developer is the hero of our story. We&#39;re looking for a Senior Manager, Brand Marketing to lead it into its next chapter. Our team is small by design, the category is at an inflection point, and you&#39;ll be close to the decisions that shape what comes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategic individual contributor role on the Content team, reporting to the Senior Director of Marketing and Communications. You&#39;ll work every day with Content and Visual Design, which together act as an in-house agency for the rest of marketing. You&#39;ll be the steward of our customer and of our copy. We&#39;re investing in brand, and you&#39;ll have a focused budget and leadership behind you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A day might start with a launch headline that isn&#39;t landing and an hour showing the writer why. Then a working session with the Senior Creative Director on a campaign concept, a pass on the narrative leadership will use with the company, and a late check on what AI assistants are telling developers about us. The next day looks different.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guide the brand.&lt;/strong&gt; Shape our strategy, positioning, and narrative through this next chapter. Start with what we&#39;ve built, and help us see where it should evolve as the way software gets built changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the company&#39;s voice.&lt;/strong&gt; Choose when to lead with personality and when to lead with proof. Own our positioning in the market and carry the story across every global touchpoint from our homepage, holistic web experience, events, sales comms and paid advertising. Show its impact through conversion rates and other measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steward our copy.&lt;/strong&gt; Be the final read on the work that matters most, from campaign concepts to launch headlines to sales decks. Use one test: would an engineer here send it to a friend? Write the biggest pieces yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable marketing.&lt;/strong&gt; Content is produced across all of marketing, so enabling writers is as much your job as reviewing their work. Review fewer things, and make the rest better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a creative partner.&lt;/strong&gt; Work side by side with Visual Design from the first idea. Be a generous brainstorm partner who builds on rough concepts, and give feedback that makes the work better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know who we are and what we do.&lt;/strong&gt; Learn the product, the company, and the developers we serve. Spend time with the people who build and sell CircleCI, follow where developers ta

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior GTM Strategy and Operations Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you passionate about driving growth and operational excellence? If you thrive in a dynamic environment where strategy meets execution, this role is for you! We’re hiring a Senior GTM Strategy and Operations Manager to develop and execute strategies that enhance growth, improve efficiency, and foster valuable partnerships. This is a high-visibility, high-impact role that shapes how we grow revenue and go-to-market strategies. This role reports directly to the Director of GTM Strategy and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The GTM Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is dedicated to developing and executing strategic initiatives that drive growth and operational efficiency across the company. We work collaboratively with departments such as marketing, sales, finance, product management, and customer success to ensure alignment and drive impactful results. Our team prioritizes data-driven decision-making, continuous improvement, and customer engagement to refine our approach and maximize impact. We value agility and aim to deliver measurable results quickly while fostering a culture of innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics Leadership:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development and maintenance of comprehensive dashboards and reports that provide actionable insights on key performance indicators (KPIs) and operational metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute projects to identify trends, opportunities, and areas for improvement across all GTM to provide data-driven recommendations for strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecasting and Planning:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the annual and quarterly revenue planning process, establishing and tracking quotas and attainment, partnering with Finance and Sales leadership to develop bottoms-up forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dynamic forecasting models that incorporate pipeline, bookings, expansion, and churn signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive monthly and quarterly business reviews with actionable analysis and clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations Management:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize end-to-end GTM processes, including lead management, opportunity management, and customer lifecycle workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement best practices for data management, ensuring data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process gaps and drive cross-functional initiatives to close them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deploy AI agents to automate recurring workflows, streamline key business reporting, and so the team can focus on strategic work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
